        infrastructure
      </li>
      <li>led a performance optimisation project for customers in mainland China</li>
      <li>standardised front end application architecture and software stack for ~15 teams, ~50 apps</li>
      <li>devised technical roadmap and initial estimates for multi-year, group-wide UX uplift initiative</li>
      <li>programmed practice meetings, skills training, and internal resources</li>
      <li>provided informal mentorship to engineers across the organisation</li>
      <li>evolved Culture Amp's front end coding interview over multiple generations</li>
      <li>
        produced countless internal engineering standards, guides, RFCs, decision-making documents, and business cases
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
    <h3>
      <span><a href="https://www.avalanche.com.au">Avalanche &amp; AVG AU/NZ</a>: Chief Technology Officer</span>
      <span class="timespan">2012 → 2015</span>
    </h3>

    <p>
      I began my tenure at Avalanche leading Information Technology and internal software development for AVG AU/NZ, a
      direct-to-consumer software sales business that was a wholly-owned subsidiary of Avalanche. This included delivery
      leadership for a small engineering team building the company’s in-house CRM and e-commerce platform. During my
      tenure, the business was acquired by AVG Technologies B.V., for which I facilitated the integration of the
      business into AVG’s global technology infrastructure.
    </p>
    <p>
      I then transitioned to leading the engineering of Avalanche’s pre-seed startup initiatives:
      <a href="https://breachalarm.com">BreachAlarm</a> (née Should I Change My Password, a password leak notification
      service similar to <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com">Have I Been Pwned</a>), Sit the Test (an online test
      authoring and delivery platform), and Send a Slab (a gift-delivery service based on the Australian tradition of
      giving a "slab" of beer as thanks).
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>led small engineering teams of 2-3 people on the above projects</li>
      <li>designed the systems architecture for BreachAlarm, Sit the Test, and Send a Slab</li>
      <li>implemented AWS continuous delivery and infrastructure automation (CircleCI, Chef)</li>
      <li>partnered with the business owner and executives on strategic initiatives</li>
      <li>
        ran internal IT (literally fixed the printer when it broke) and managed Windows network servers for an office of
        ~50 people
      </li>
      <li>trained the executive team on the Getting Things Done (GTD) personal productivity framework</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
