    <p>
      The Melbourne Pen &amp; Stationery Show is Australia’s premier event for lovers of fine writing instruments,
      stationery, and craftsmanship, bringing the pen community together every year since 1998 (except 2020-2021). It is
      run as a nonprofit incorporated association by a small group of volunteers. I joined the committee in 2023 and was
      elected President in 2025.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apart from leading the effort to organise the annual event, I have also built and maintained the event’s website
      and other technical systems.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        formed the new committee that moved the show from its longtime home in the suburbs to a city-centre venue,
        <a href="https://melbpenshow.com.au/news/2025-10-29-2025-mpss-by-the-numbers/">
          increasing attendance to 2.5× the previous record
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        replaced the show’s aging single-page web brochure with a modern, responsive website backed by CloudCannon
        Git-based CMS and Eleventy static site generator – the best pen show website in the world
      </li>
      <li>
        fully automated the show’s charity raffle with custom software that tracks sold tickets, awards prizes, and
        notifies winners
      </li>
    </ul>
